# .claude file for Mutual Aid Community App
# This file provides context and guidance for Claude Code when working on this project

project_name: "Mutual Aid Community App"
description: |
  A privacy-first, offline-capable mutual aid network application that enables 
  community members to request and offer help through Bluetooth Low Energy mesh networking.
  
  Core principles:
  - Privacy by design (no central server, encrypted coordination)
  - Dignity-preserving (no charity dynamics, mutual exchange)
  - Accessible (works for all literacy levels, ages, abilities)
  - Offline-first (BLE mesh, works without internet)
  - No free-text (categorical system prevents abuse)
  - Community-driven (patterns emerge organically, not algorithmically)

technology_stack:
  mobile:
    - React Native (cross-platform iOS/Android)
    - TypeScript (type safety)
    - libsodium (encryption via react-native-sodium)
    - react-native-ble-manager (Bluetooth LE)
    - AsyncStorage (local data persistence)
    - react-native-maps (OpenStreetMap via Mapbox)
  
  desktop:
    - Electron (optional, for broader access)
  
  data:
    - No backend/server
    - All data stored locally
    - Messages broadcast via BLE mesh
    - JSON schema for message format

key_features:
  - Create requests (NEED messages)
  - Create offers (OFFER messages)
  - Browse nearby requests/offers
  - Encrypted coordination between parties
  - Optional broker/intermediary system
  - Multi-payload encryption (share with multiple recipients)
  - Adaptive privacy (location precision based on network density)
  - Good news broadcasts (anonymous completion announcements)
  - QR code sharing for network growth
  - Wizard-based UI for ease of use

architecture:
  message_types:
    - NEED: Request for help
    - OFFER: Offer to help
    - COORDINATION: Private coordination between matched parties
    - BROKER_ACCESS: Grant broker access to coordination
    - COMPLETION: Anonymous "good news" broadcast
    - REVOCATION: Revoke broker access
  
  privacy_model:
    - Public broadcast: Category, approximate location/time, quantity
    - Private coordination: Exact location, contact name, specific times
    - Multi-recipient encryption: Different details to different parties
    - No persistent identity: New keys per message
    - Message flooding: Relay messages for plausible deniability
  
  network:
    - BLE mesh (100m range per hop)
    - Store-and-forward relay
    - No hop count preserved (privacy)
    - Message expiration (24-48 hours)
    - Offline queue with sync

directory_structure: |
  mutual-aid-app/
